{"diagnosis": "Loopback 0xa5 never asserts recv_buf_valid so sim traps on uart timeout with no byte received. Expected recv_state to advance through data bits to state 10 to copy recv_pattern to recv_buf_data, but it remains stuck. Root cause is line 99 `recv_state <= recv_state + 0` in the default case which never increments recv_state and recv_divcnt logic never reaches state 10.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@
 			default: begin
 				if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 					recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
-					recv_state <= recv_state + 0;
+					recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 					recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
 			end", "expected": "tohost PASS (vs FAIL 0xdead), loopback 0xa5 received with recv_buf_valid set, no uart timeout"}

